Bharadvāja follows like father and shows the way --- Bharadvāja bids raft swift Kālindī Yamunā --- Bids greet green Śyāma banyan of adepts --- Bids walk one krōśa to blue Badarī bamboo wood --- Shows pleasant fire-free path then turns back --- Rāma leads Sītā first to Kālindī --- Brothers bind raft and cut pleasant seat for Sītā --- Rāma lifts shy Sītā onto raft and crosses Yamunā --- Leave raft and greet Śyāma as Sītā prays for mothers --- Walk one krōśa slaying deer to river-bank dwelling
